<div class="non-normative">

# Introduction # {#sctn-intro}

*This section is non-normative.*

This specification defines functionality allowing a native application to
handle payment requests that originate on the web on behalf of users. Such
applications are referred to as [=native-app payment handlers=]. [=Native-app
payment handlers=] are accessed via an abstract "provider", the [=native
payment app provider model=], to avoid having to specify details of specific
operating systems or other integrations. The [=native payment app provider
model=] has abstract operations which can be supported by concrete providers.

</div>

# Native-app payment handlers # {#sctn-native-app-payment-handler}

A <dfn>native-app payment handler</dfn> is a [=payment handler=], as defined in
[[payment-request]], that is backed by some underlying [=native payment app=]
that can be accessed via a [=native payment app provider=].

This section describes the steps the user agent MUST take when intermediating
between a {{PaymentRequest}} object and one or more [=native payment apps=] from
a single [=native payment app provider=].

## Can make payment algorithm ## {#sctn-can-make-payment-algorithm}

When performing step 8.2. of the [=can make payment algorithm=] from
[[payment-request]] for a [=payment method identifier=] |identifier|, the
user agent MUST perform the following steps:

1. For each available [=native payment app provider=], |provider|:

    1. [=Get the list of native payment apps=] known to |provider|. Let the
         result be |paymentApps|.

    1. For each |paymentApp| in |paymentApps|:

         1. If |paymentApp| [=is allowed to handle the payment method
              identifier=] |identifier|, resolve `hasHandlerPromise` with `true`
              and terminate any remaining steps.

## The show() method ## {#sctn-show-method}

When performing step 17.5. of the {{PaymentRequest/show|PaymentRequest.show()}}
method, the user agent MUST perform the following steps:

1. For each available [=native payment app provider=], |provider|:

    1. [=Get the list of native payment apps=] known to |provider|. Let the
         result be |paymentApps|.

    1. For each |paymentApp| in |paymentApps|:

         1. If |paymentApp| [=is allowed to handle the payment method
              identifier=] |identifier|, create a [=native-app payment handler=]
              for |paymentApp| and append it to the list of registered payment
              handlers.

When a [=native-app payment handler=] is selected by the user (steps 19-24 of
the show() algorithm), the user agent MUST [=invoke the native payment app=]
corresponding to the selected [=native-app payment handler=].

ISSUE: The [[payment-request]] spec is quite vague about what data is or should
be passed to an invoked payment handler. We should try to be more specific.

NOTE: The invoked payment app will ultimately communicate a result back to the
user agent, either by [=indicating success=], [=indicating user cancellation=],
or [=indicating internal error=].

## Steps to check if a payment can be made ## {#sctn-steps-to-check-if-a-payment-can-be-made}

The [=steps to check if a payment can be made=] for a [=native-app payment
handler=] and JSON-serialized {{PaymentMethodData/data|PaymentMethodData.data}}
object are:

1. Return `true`.

NOTE: No steps are necessary here. We have already verified the payment
handler's claims in [[#sctn-show-method]] and made sure that they match the
identifier. No additional filtering is needed based on the serialized
{{PaymentMethodData/data}}.

## Steps to respond to a payment request ## {#sctn-steps-to-respond-to-a-payment-request}

The [=steps to respond to a payment request=] for a [=native-app payment
handler=], |handler|, are:

1. Let |app| be the underlying [=native payment app=] for |handler|.

1. [=Retrieve the converted result details=] for |app|, and return it.

## Verifying native-app payment handler claims ## {#sctn-verifying-app-claims}

[=Native payment apps=] have both a [=claimed payment method identifier=] and a
set of [=claimed third-party origins=].  Verification of these claims relies
upon the payment and application manifests specified in
[[payment-method-manifest]].

ISSUE: Should we allow for alternate methods to verify the claims, to support
cases like payment apps built into the browser?

Given a [=payment method identifier=], |identifier|, and a [=native payment
app=], |app|, the following steps determine if |app| <dfn>is allowed to handle
the payment method identifier</dfn> |identifier|:

1. If |identifier| is not a [=URL-based payment method identifier=], return
     `false`.

1. Let |paymentMethodManifest| be the [=ingest payment method
     manifests|ingested=] and [=parsed payment method manifest|parsed=]
     [=payment method manifest=] for |identifier|.

1. Let |claimedIdentifier| be the [=claimed payment method identifier=]
    for |app|.

1. If |claimedIdentifier| is equal to |identifier|, then,

    1. For each [=default application=], |defaultApp|, in |paymentMethodManifest|,

        1. Let |appManifest| be the [=application manifest=] for |defaultApp|.

            ISSUE: Have the payment method manifest spec cache the web-app manifests.

        1. If |app| [=is a related application=] for |appManifest|, return `true`.

    1. Return `false`.

1. Otherwise,

    1. Let |claimedOrigins| be the [=claimed third-party origins=] for |app|.

    1. If none of the |claimedOrigins| [=match the origins allowed for a
        payment method identifier|match the origins allowed for=] |identifier|,
        return `false`.

    1. Let |claimedPaymentMethodManifest| be the [=ingest payment method
        manifests|ingested=] and [=parsed payment method manifest|parsed=]
        [=payment method manifest=] for |claimedIdentifier|.

    1. For each [=default application=], |defaultApp|, in
        |claimedPaymentMethodManifest|,

        1. Let |appManifest| be the [=application manifest=] for |defaultApp|.

            ISSUE: Have the payment method manifest spec cache the web-app manifests.

        1. If |app| [=is a related application=] for |appManifest|, return `true`.

    1. Return `false`.


## Match origins allowed for a payment method identifier ## {#sctn-match-origins}

ISSUE: This algorithm should probably exist in [[payment-method-manifest]]
       rather than here.

To determine if a [=set=] of [=origins=], |claimedOrigins|, <dfn>match the
origins allowed for a payment method identifier</dfn>, |identifier|, run the
following steps:

1. Let |paymentMethodManifest| be the [=ingest payment method
     manifests|ingested=] and [=parsed payment method manifest|parsed=]
     [=payment method manifest=] for |identifier|.

1. For each [=origin=] |claimedOrigin| in |claimedOrigins|:

    1. If |claimedOrigin| is equal to |identifier|'s [=origin=], return `true`.

             ISSUE: Is this right? The |identifier| can cause a redirect, so
             what should we be checking against?

    1. If |paymentMethodManifest|'s [=supported origins=] is the string `'*'`,
        return `true`.

    1. If |paymentMethodManifest|'s [=supported origins=] contains
        |claimedOrigin|, return `true`.

        NOTE: [=Supported origins=] can either be the string "*", or an [=set=]
        of [=origins=].

1. Return `false`.

# Native payment app provider model # {#sctn-native-payment-app-model}

The [=native-app payment handler=] API implies a specific abstract functional
model through which the user agent can interact with [=native payment apps=].
This section describes that model.

The <dfn>native payment app provider model</dfn> is an abstract functional
model which describes the behavior of some <dfn>native payment app
provider</dfn> (e.g., the operating system) that facilitates access to
underlying [=native payment apps=]. <dfn>Native payment apps</dfn> are
deliberately loosely defined, simply as sorm form of application that is not a
web-based application within the scope of this user agent.

NOTE: For payment applications that are web-based within the scope of this user
agent, see [[!web-based-payment-handler]].

Providers MAY implement and expose this abstract model in any way desired, as
long as the normative requirements of the model are met. See
[[#sctn-examples]].

## Returning a list of [=native payment apps=] ## {#sctn-returning-list}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a method by which the user agent
can <dfn>get the list of native payment apps</dfn> known to the provider.

## Claiming a method URL ## {#sctn-claiming-method-url}

Given a [=native payment app=], |app|, a [=native payment app provider=] MUST
provide a method by which the user agent can get the <dfn>claimed payment
method identifier</dfn> for |app|. This is a [=url-based payment method
identifier=] that |app| claims it is associated with, and for which the
[=payment method manifest=] will list some [=default application=] that has
|app| as a [=related application=]. The user agent MUST verify this claim (see
[[#sctn-verifying-app-claims]]).

## Claiming a set of origins ## {#sctn-claiming-origins}

Given a [=native payment app=], |app|, a [=native payment app provider=] MUST
provide a method by which the user agent can get the <dfn>claimed third-party
origins</dfn>. This is a [=set=] of [=origins=] that the [=native payment app=]
claims that it has the right to act on behalf of, though user agents MUST
verify that against the origin (see [[#sctn-verifying-app-claims]]).

## Checking if a [=native payment app=] is a related application for a web app manifest ## {#sctn-related-application}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a method by which the user agent
can check if a [=native payment app=] <dfn>is a related application</dfn> for a
[=application manifest|web app manifest=]. This method MAY utilize the
information contained in the [=related applications=], such as the [=id=],
[=platform=], or [=fingerprints=] of each specified [=external application
resource=].

## Determining if a [=native payment app=] can handle a {{PaymentRequest}} ## {#sctn-hasenrolled-instrument}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a method by which the user agent
can check if a [=native payment app=] is <dfn export>able to handle a payment
request</dfn>. In order to support this functionality, the user agent MAY pass
information about the specific {{PaymentRequest}} to the [=native payment
app=], but considerations SHOULD be made regarding user privacy.

NOTE: This functionality is used to answer the `hasEnrolledInstrument` method
on {{PaymentRequest}}, which was removed from the [[payment-request]]
specification but is still shipping in multiple browser engines.

ISSUE: We should speak to the privacy issues in a privacy section.

## Invoking a [=native payment app=] ## {#sctn-invoking}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a method by which the user agent
can <dfn>invoke the native payment app</dfn> for a given [=native payment
app=]. When run, this method MUST pass control of the current experience over
to the invoked [=native payment app=], until such times as the native payment
app [=indicates success=], [=indicates user cancellation=], or [=indicates internal
error=].

Depending on the capabilities of the [=native payment app provider=], the
invoked app MAY be displayed partially over the user agent window (to improve
user context and understanding of the flow).

ISSUE: We should speak to the privacy issues in a privacy section.

## Communicating with an invoked [=native payment app=] ## {#sctn-dynamic-updates}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a method by which the user agent
can <dfn export>communicate with an invoked payment app</dfn>.

ISSUE: This needs fleshed out, to include; notifying that the payment method
has changed, notifying that the shipping address or options have changed,
notifying that payer details have changed. Also, what capabilty needs to be
defined at the payment handler level rather than in the model.

## Indicating success of an invoked [=native payment app=] ## {#sctn-indicating-success}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a way for an invoked [=native
payment app=] to <dfn>indicate success</dfn> back to the user agent. When this
occurs, the user agent MUST run the [=user accepts the payment request
algorithm=] from [[payment-request]].

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST also provide a way for the user agent to
<dfn>retrieve the converted result details</dfn> for an invoked [=native payment
app=] that has [=indicated success=]. This must be converted to a form suitable
for the user agent to place in the {{PaymentResponse/details}} field of the
response that will be returned from {{PaymentRequest/show()}}.

## Indicating user cancel from an invoked [=native payment app=] ## {#sctn-indicating-user-cancel}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a way for an invoked [=native
payment app=] to <dfn>indicate user cancellation</dfn> back to the user agent.
When this occurs, the user agent MUST run the [=user aborts the payment request
algorithm=] from [[payment-request]].

## Indicating internal error from an invoked [=native payment app=] ## {#sctn-indicating-internal-error}

A [=native payment app provider=] MUST provide a way for an invoked [=native
payment app=] to <dfn>indicate internal error</dfn> back to the user agent.
When this occurs, the user agent MUST run the [=payment handler indicates an
internal error algorithm=] from [[payment-request]].

